        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Good point — sitemap.xml (generated at build time, not checked into the repo) is exhaustive and meant for traditional search-engine crawlers indexing every URL. `llms.txt` serves a different purpose: it's a small, curated, human-picked index (~20-30 links out of ~150 generated doc pages) meant to fit in an LLM's context window and point it to the most useful pages first, following the https://llmstxt.org/ convention. The two are complementary rather than redundant — sitemap.xml says \"here's everything,\" llms.txt says \"here's what matters most, start here.\" Happy to trim the list further or adjust structure if that would help review.",
